---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: "Extending kuwai",
      url: "https://kuwai.kitsunekode.in/extending/",
      description: "Path B-Lite declarative panels and safe extension without untrusted QML.",
      isPartOf: { "@id": "https://kuwai.kitsunekode.in/#website" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://kuwai.kitsunekode.in/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Extending", item: "https://kuwai.kitsunekode.in/extending/" }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Extending kuwai: Path B-Lite panels"
  description="Safe declarative JSON panels for kuwai: no untrusted QML, only built-in primitives."
  canonicalPath="/extending/"
  ogImage="/og-image.png"
  solidHeader={true}
  schemaJson={schema}
>
  <main class="subpage-main">
    <section class="subpage-head">
      <div class="container">
        <h1 class="subpage-title">Extending kuwai</h1>
        <p class="section-intro">
          kuwai's shell is Quickshell QML, but anything you add from outside must not execute arbitrary code. Path B-Lite is the supported way to ship small island panels as data, not as downloaded QML.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Path B-Lite (declarative JSON)</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">A panel definition is a JSON document validated against kuwai's schema. The shell renders it with the same <code>Card</code>, <code>Button</code>, <code>SettingsRow</code>, and <code>Label</code> primitives every built-in panel uses. Text fields are plain text; links go through the same safe opener as notifications.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <h3>What you can describe</h3>
          <ul class="plain-list">
            <li>Title, sections, and rows with labels and detail strings.</li>
            <li>Actions that call known island targets (open launcher, settings page, or an approved URL).</li>
            <li>Read-only status lines fed from local JSON the shell already trusts.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
          <h3>What is refused</h3>
          <ul class="plain-list">
            <li>Arbitrary QML, JavaScript, or shell hooks inside the panel file.</li>
            <li>Markup in user-visible strings (everything is <code>Text.PlainText</code>).</li>
            <li>Commands pasted into scripts; actions are enumerated, not free-form.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="section-footnote">
          Panel files are intended to live under <code>~/.config/kuwai/panels/</code> once the loader lands in the shell. Until then, fork the repository and add a full QML module if you need behaviour that JSON cannot express.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Themes from Omarchy</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Bring colours from an Omarchy theme without running its install hooks. Only <code>colors.toml</code> is read; hex values must be <code>#RRGGBB</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <pre class="terminal-code"><code>kuwai-look import-omarchy ~/path/to/omarchy-theme --dry-run
kuwai-look import-omarchy ~/path/to/omarchy-theme my-theme</code></pre>
        <p class="section-intro">The command writes <code>palette.toml</code> and <code>theme.toml</code> into <code>~/.local/share/kuwai-data/themes/</code>. Scripts and hooks beside <code>colors.toml</code> are ignored.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Further reading</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/KitsuneKode/kuwai/blob/main/docs/manual/looks.md" class="inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Looks and kuwai-look</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/KitsuneKode/kuwai/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md" class="inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Design tokens</a></li>
          <li><a href="/island/" class="inline-link">Island and capsules</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>